---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../styles/components.css';
const schema = {"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "Product", "name": "Garden Rooms", "description": "Insulated underground garden rooms", "brand": {"@type": "Brand", "name": "Revonia"}, "offers": {"@type": "AggregateOffer", "priceCurrency": "GBP", "lowPrice": "45000", "offerCount": 1}, "manufacturer": {"@type": "Organization", "name": "Luxury Modules", "url": "https://luxurymodules.co.uk", "description": "Official UK partner of Revonia. Turnkey vaulted living spaces, cellars and saunas."}};
---
<Layout title="Garden Rooms: Insulated & Underground | Luxury Modules" description="A garden room that outlives the house: earth-sheltered, insulated as standard and built for a century of use. Explore designs, sizes and from-pricing." schema={schema}>
<div class="pagehero">
  <p class="kicker">Use Case · Living</p>
  <h1>Garden rooms designed to disappear</h1>
  <p>A garden room that outlives the house: earth-sheltered, insulated as standard and built for a century of use. From above, lawn and planting. Inside, a vaulted room flooded with daylight.</p>
  <div class="price-anchor">From £45,000</div>
  <div style="margin-top:28px"><a class="btn" href="/book-a-call/">Book a Scoping Call</a> <a class="btn ghost" href="#brochure" style="margin-left:8px">Download Brochure</a></div>
</div>
<div class="strip">Official UK Partner of <b>Revonia</b> &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; <b>1,500+</b> projects across Europe &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; <b>25-year</b> structural warranty &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; Planning <b>handled for you</b></div>
<div class="imgph hero"><img class="real" src="/images/garden-room-exterior.jpg" alt="Insulated garden room with arched glazing set into a planted garden bank"><span class="lbl">ASSET: garden-room-exterior.jpg — final</span></div>
<section><div class="wrap">
  <p class="kicker">The Fast Truth</p><h2>Insulated as standard, not as an upgrade</h2><div class="gold-rule"></div>
  <p class="lead">Ask a typical garden room supplier what insulation costs extra, then read their spec sheet's small print. Ours is simpler: vaulted concrete wrapped in earth, geomembrane waterproofing, triple-glazed wooden doors and windows and underfloor heating, on every build, at the listed from-price. An insulated garden room is not our premium tier — it is the only thing we make.</p>
</div></section>

<section class="navy-band"><div class="wrap">
  <p class="kicker">One Room, Many Lives</p><h2>What can a garden room be?</h2><div class="gold-rule"></div>
  <div class="grid cols4">
    <div class="card"><div class="body"><h3>An office</h3><p>Year-round working space, call-quality quiet. <a href="/spaces/garden-office/" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Garden office &rarr;</a></p></div></div>
    <div class="card"><div class="body"><h3>A gym</h3><p>Stable temperature, real floor loading. <a href="/spaces/garden-gym/" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Garden gym &rarr;</a></p></div></div>
    <div class="card"><div class="body"><h3>An annexe</h3><p>Independent living, steps from the house. <a href="/spaces/garden-annexe/" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Granny annexe &rarr;</a></p></div></div>
    <div class="card"><div class="body"><h3>A retreat</h3><p>Sauna, spa or snug. <a href="/products/cave-saunas/" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Cave saunas &rarr;</a></p></div></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section><div class="wrap">
  <p class="kicker">The Comparison</p><h2>Garden room or extension?</h2><div class="gold-rule"></div>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table class="spec">
    <tr><th></th><th>Underground garden room</th><th>House extension</th></tr>
    <tr><td>Disruption</td><td>Garden works only; you stay in the house untouched</td><td>Months of builders through the kitchen</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Timeline</td><td>Install in days once consented; ~26 weeks end to end</td><td>Commonly 9–18 months design to finish</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Planning</td><td>Often permitted development; consent handled by us when needed</td><td>Almost always needs full consent, managed by you</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Cost certainty</td><td>Turnkey from-price; site variables settled before contract</td><td>Overruns are the norm, not the exception</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Garden</td><td>Kept — the room hides under it</td><td>Lost to footprint</td></tr>
  </table></div>
</div></section>

<section style="background:#efe9db"><div class="wrap">
  <p class="kicker">Ranges</p><h2>Sizes, ranges and from-prices</h2><div class="gold-rule"></div>
  <p class="lead" style="margin-bottom:26px"><a href="/products/small-living-spaces/" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Small Living 10–29m&sup2;</a> from &pound;45,000 &middot; <a href="/products/medium-living-spaces/" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Medium Living 30–40m&sup2;</a> from &pound;99,000 &middot; <a href="/products/large-living-spaces/" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Large Living 60–80m&sup2;</a> from &pound;199,000. Full detail on the <a href="/pricing/" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">pricing page</a>.</p>
</div></section>

<section><div class="wrap">
  <p class="kicker">The Rules</p><h2>Do you need planning permission?</h2><div class="gold-rule"></div>
  <p class="lead" style="margin-bottom:26px">Usually not — most garden rooms fall within permitted development. The exceptions, sizes and height rules are in the <a href="/planning-permission/" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">planning guide</a>, and when consent is needed, we handle it.</p>
</div></section>
<section style="background:#efe9db"><div class="wrap">
  <p class="kicker">FAQ</p><h2>Your questions, answered</h2><div class="gold-rule"></div>
  <div class="faq-item"><h3>Do garden rooms add value?</h3><p>A permanent insulated structure with a 25-year warranty is an asset, not a depreciating outbuilding. Agents typically treat quality garden rooms as adding usable square-metreage.</p></div><div class="faq-item"><h3>Can you live in a garden room?</h3><p>Sleeping accommodation changes the planning position — it becomes ancillary residential use. Our annexe page and planning guide cover exactly when that is straightforward.</p></div><div class="faq-item"><h3>Are garden rooms worth it?</h3><p>If a timber cabin would do, buy a timber cabin. Ours are for people who want a room that performs like the house and outlives it.</p></div>
  <p style="margin-top:18px;font-size:14.5px">More questions? <a href="/faq/" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">See the full FAQ</a>.</p>
</div></section><section class="ctaband" id="cta">
  <h2>A room your garden keeps secret</h2>
  <p>Book a scoping call, or download the brochure and browse every design first.</p>
  <div class="btns"><a class="btn" href="/book-a-call/">Book a Scoping Call</a><a class="btn ghost" href="#brochure">Download the Brochure</a></div>
  
  <!-- BUILD NOTE: brochure CTA = HubSpot email-only form (hidden fields: product_interest, product_range, audience_type, source_page_url). Scoping CTA -> contact.html until /book-a-call/ with calendar embed exists. -->
</section>
</Layout>
